PR #2660  overall: potential_risk
Spec: Privilege-mode filtering on cycle/instret counters must be enforced exactly: no increments in inhibited modes, unimplemented-mode bits must be read-only zero, exception-causing instructions must not increment instret, and xRET must only increment if the originating mode is non-inhibited — otherwise execution metadata leaks across privilege boundaries
  [RISK] lib/sbi/sbi_domain_context.c:102-169  switch_to_next_domain_context
      The hart_context struct (lines 24-58) and the domain context save/restore path (lines 130-146) do NOT include mcyclecfg/minstretcfg CSRs (Smcntrpmf). Only scounteren is saved/restored (line 142), which gates S-mode read access to counters but does NOT save/restore the counter inhibit configuration itself. If two domains have different Smcntrpmf inhibit profiles (e.g. domain A expects S-mode inhibited, domain B does not), the mcyclecfg/minstretcfg CSRs persist unswitched across domain boundaries, allowing counter deltas to leak execution-timing metadata between domains at M-mode level. The implicit invariant that 'all domains share identical Smcntrpmf configurations' or 'no domain relies on inhibit settings for isolation' is not enforced in code. The PR's addition of __sbi_sfence_vma_all() at line 140 (TLB flush after SATP swap) is itself compliant but addresses a separate TLB-coherence concern, not Smcntrpmf.
  [OK] include/sbi/sbi_tlb.h:57-57  __sbi_sfence_vma_all
      Function declaration of __sbi_sfence_vma_all() — correctly declared void with no Smcntrpmf implications. This is a necessary build dependency for the PR's TLB flush call site.
  [OK] lib/sbi/sbi_tlb.c:32-35  __sbi_sfence_vma_all
      Executes sfence.vma inline assembly — the architecturally correct instruction for flushing all hart-local TLB entries. This is exactly what the RISC-V privileged spec requires after a SATP mode switch. No Smcntrpmf issues.

